WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.740
The year of the Batman reveals continues.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:07.000
The first trailer for the second season of
the DC Universe series Titans has been released,

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.660
and it gives fans their first look at Iain
Glen's Bruce Wayne and, as an added bonus,

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.200
Esai Morales' Deathstroke, canonically the
Titans' most persistent nemesis.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.740
Titans is the inaugural original series effort
for DC Universe, and its first season racked

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:24.250
up accolades for its dark yet humorous take
on the Teen Titans, DC's classic superhero

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.800
team led by Dick Grayson, better known as
Robin.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.500
"F--- Batman."

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.480
During the first season, the rest of the team
included Rachel Roth, or Raven, the alien

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.079
Koriand'r, a.k.a. Starfire, and Gar Logan,
otherwise known as Beast Boy.

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:43.860
The group also crossed paths with Donna Troy,
also known as Wonder Girl, Hank Hall, a.k.a.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.370
Hawk, and Dawn Granger, a.k.a. Dove, all of
whom can be spotted briefly in the trailer

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:49.240
for season 2.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.120
Fans had an inkling that Bruce Wayne would
be a part of this new season; at the conclusion

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.500
of season 1, Robin endured an episode-long
hallucination in which he, five years in the

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.740
future, was forced to track down and kill
an out-of-control Batman.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.290
The elaborate hallucination was an effort
on the part of the demon Trigon, Rachel's

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.960
father, to take control of Grayson's mortal
form.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.620
It's a goal he seems to accomplish at the
season's end but we'll have to wait and see

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.460
how that plays out.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.540
Fans had been psyched to catch a glimpse of
Glen as Wayne, and we got one, however brief.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:19.050
Well, we can report that he looks the part,
although we're not so sure that he exactly

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.380
sounds like the Dark Knight.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.560
"See you made the news with your old Titans
friends… new ones too."

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.100
Glen is Scottish, and we're sure that in his
mind, he's doing a flawless American accent

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.280
but to American ears, it sounds a little bit
dodgy.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.960
Aside from Wayne, the spot also introduces
viewers to Drew Van Acker's Aqualad and Chelsea

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.580
T. Zhang's Ravager and, at its conclusion,
Deathstroke, standing bathed in shadow at

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.280
the end of a dark, foreboding hallway.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:47.300
Obviously, we don't get a good look at the
villain's costume, but he sure cuts a badass,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.630
menacing figure, and we're sure that's not
the only thing he'll be cutting; he didn't

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.040
bring along those swords for nothing.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:55.760
Also, in a moment fans have been waiting for
since it was teased in the post-credits stinger

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.680
of the season 1 finale, we get a look at Joshua
Orpin's Superboy, and Krypto, the Super-Dog.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.340
We don't get to see the pooch in action, but
we're thinking that the show's producers didn't

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.580
want to tip their hand too soon.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.780
Will he be wearing a cape when he bounds into
action?

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.800
That would really be the icing on the cake.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.740
If, like us, you're a big fan of the Dark
Knight, this year has been and will continue

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:17.570
to be a very good one in terms of giving us
more live-action Batmen than you can shake

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.580
a Batarang at.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.890
First, the series finale of Gotham finally
gave us that show's version of the Caped Crusader,

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:26.020
something we'd all been anticipating for the
entirety of the show's run.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.970
September will see the premiere of Titans'
second season, and in December, the CW's Arrowverse

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:35.680
will stage another of its huge crossover events,
one with a name that every single DC fan will

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.480
recognize: "Crisis on Infinite Earths."

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.640
Cast in the role of Bruce Wayne for the multiverse
mashup: Kevin Conroy, who has provided the

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.360
voice of the character in animated series,
features, and video games for over two decades.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:51.120
Many Bat-fans, in fact, believe his interpretation
of Bruce Wayne to be the definitive one, and

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.500
you'll get no argument from us.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:57.430
DC Universe made serious waves with its cancellation
of Swamp Thing after only one episode of its

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:01.400
truncated first season had aired, but any
rumblings that the service may be in danger

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.430
of folding have seemingly been put to rest,
with Doom Patrol recently renewed for a second

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.690
season, an amazingly not-safe-for-work trailer
for the animated Harley Quinn series, and

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.090
now, our first look at what appears to be
a smashing new season for Titans.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.540
We'll keep our ears to the ground for any
news concerning the streamer's slate of original

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.560
series, and keep you up to speed.

